  "track.storage.m.prefs.saved.mem": "memory only",
  "track.storage.m.prefs.saved.pending": "being written to disk",
  "track.storage.m.prefs.saved.disk": "on disk, confirmed",
  "track.storage.m.prefs.saved.unknown": "unknown: the failure was not reported",
  "track.storage.cap.prefs": "The main thread on top, the IO thread below, the file on the right. The arrow shows who is writing to disk; a red outline marks a blocked main thread or a swallowed error.",
  "track.storage.m.prefs.s.commit.s1.title": "Tap the dark theme switch: commit() on main",
  "track.storage.m.prefs.s.commit.s1.explain": "onClick runs on the main thread and calls commit(). commit updates the in-memory copy and writes to disk within the call, returning only when the write is done.",
  "track.storage.m.prefs.ev.commit.s1": "Tap the dark theme switch: commit() on main",
  "track.storage.m.prefs.s.commit.s2.title": "The main thread waits for the whole file",
  "track.storage.m.prefs.s.commit.s2.explain": "In the AOSP code, every write rewrites the whole XML file and then syncs it. Meanwhile main draws no frames and handles no touches.",
  "track.storage.m.prefs.ev.commit.s2": "The main thread waits for the whole file",
  "track.storage.m.prefs.s.commit.s3.title": "Slow storage: main is blocked long, ANR risk",
  "track.storage.m.prefs.s.commit.s3.explain": "A cheap device, storage busy (another app is updating). The write takes hundreds of milliseconds or more. The screen freezes; if a touch goes unanswered for 5 seconds, the system shows an ANR.",
  "track.storage.m.prefs.ev.commit.s3": "Slow storage: main is blocked long, ANR risk",
  "track.storage.m.prefs.s.commit.s4.title": "commit() returns true, and only then the screen redraws",
  "track.storage.m.prefs.s.commit.s4.explain": "The one upside: you know for sure it was saved (true) or not (false). The price is a main thread that stood still for the whole write.",
  "track.storage.m.prefs.ev.commit.s4": "commit() returns true, and only then the screen redraws",
  "track.storage.m.prefs.s.apply.s1.title": "Tap the dark theme switch: apply()",
  "track.storage.m.prefs.s.apply.s1.explain": "apply updates the in-memory copy at once and returns; the disk write is queued for another thread. Reading the key right after sees the new value.",
  "track.storage.m.prefs.ev.apply.s1": "Tap the dark theme switch: apply()",
  "track.storage.m.prefs.s.apply.s2.title": "Another thread writes the whole file, main is free",
  "track.storage.m.prefs.s.apply.s2.explain": "Still a rewrite of the whole file plus a sync, but on a background thread. The screen redraws at once.",
  "track.storage.m.prefs.ev.apply.s2": "Another thread writes the whole file, main is free",
  "track.storage.m.prefs.s.apply.s3.title": "The user goes home: main waits for the unfinished write",
  "track.storage.m.prefs.s.apply.s3.explain": "The Activity moves to onStop. The framework makes sure in-flight apply() writes finish before an Activity or Service changes state, so the main thread waits for the writer. With a slow disk, this is the ANR.",
  "track.storage.m.prefs.ev.apply.s3": "The user goes home: main waits for the unfinished write",
  "track.storage.m.prefs.s.apply.s4.title": "The write fails: nobody is told",
  "track.storage.m.prefs.s.apply.s4.explain": "Suppose the disk is full and the write fails. apply has no return value and no callback; memory says \"on\", the disk says \"not saved\". Next launch, the dark theme is gone.",
  "track.storage.m.prefs.ev.apply.s4": "The write fails: nobody is told",
  "track.storage.m.prefs.s.datastore.s1.title": "Tap the dark theme switch: edit inside viewModelScope",
  "track.storage.m.prefs.s.datastore.s1.explain": "onClick calls the ViewModel; the ViewModel launches a coroutine that calls dataStore.edit. edit is a suspend function, so main does not wait; only the coroutine pauses.",
  "track.storage.m.prefs.ev.datastore.s1": "Tap the dark theme switch: edit inside viewModelScope",
  "track.storage.m.prefs.s.datastore.s2.title": "DataStore writes on an IO thread, main is free",
  "track.storage.m.prefs.s.datastore.s2.explain": "The edit block is one read–modify–write transaction; DataStore writes the whole file (small data, no partial updates) on its own dispatcher, not on main.",
  "track.storage.m.prefs.ev.datastore.s2": "DataStore writes on an IO thread, main is free",
  "track.storage.m.prefs.s.datastore.s3.title": "The user goes home: main waits for nothing",
  "track.storage.m.prefs.s.datastore.s3.explain": "DataStore does not register its write with the Activity lifecycle queue, so onStop runs at once. The writing coroutine carries on on its own thread.",
  "track.storage.m.prefs.ev.datastore.s3": "The user goes home: main waits for nothing",
  "track.storage.m.prefs.s.datastore.s4.title": "The Flow emits the new value, the UI changes colour",
  "track.storage.m.prefs.s.datastore.s4.explain": "data is a Flow; once written it emits the new Preferences and the UI collecting it switches to the dark theme. If the write fails, the exception is thrown from edit in the coroutine that called it, catchable with try/catch.",
  "track.storage.m.prefs.ev.datastore.s4": "The Flow emits the new value, the UI changes colour",
  "track.storage.m.prefs.co.try": "Walk all four steps of each approach; count the red hatched cells in the Main thread lane.",
  "track.storage.m.prefs.co.commit.s2": "AOSP SharedPreferencesImpl: writeToFile writes the whole map with XmlUtils.writeMapXml, then syncs. [[src:aosp-sp-impl]]",
  "track.storage.m.prefs.co.commit.s3": "The ANRs page: an input event not answered within 5 seconds triggers an ANR; I/O on the main thread is a common cause. [[src:ax-anr]]",
  "track.storage.m.prefs.co.commit.s4": "The SharedPreferences.Editor page: commit returns true if the new values were successfully written to persistent storage. [[src:ax-sp-editor]]",
  "track.storage.m.prefs.co.apply.s2": "The SharedPreferences.Editor page: apply changes the in-memory copy at once and starts an asynchronous write to disk. [[src:ax-sp-editor]]",
  "track.storage.m.prefs.co.apply.s3": "The same page warns: pending apply() calls can block the main thread during lifecycle transitions, a common source of ANRs. [[src:ax-sp-editor]]",
  "track.storage.m.prefs.co.apply.s4": "The SharedPreferences.Editor page: with apply, you will not be notified of any failures. [[src:ax-sp-editor]]",
  "track.storage.m.prefs.co.datastore.s2": "The DataStore page: updateData updates transactionally, in one atomic read–modify–write; all code in the block is one transaction. [[src:ax-datastore]]",
  "track.storage.m.prefs.co.datastore.s3": "DataStore uses coroutines and Flow to store data asynchronously, consistently and transactionally. [[src:ax-datastore]]",
  "track.storage.m.prefs.co.datastore.s4": "The DataStore page: read through data, a Flow; the page advises putting reads and writes in a repository and ViewModel, not in composables. [[src:ax-datastore]]",
  "track.storage.vz.tab.pf": "Thread lanes",
  "track.storage.vz.pf.cap": "Each row is a lane, each column a step. A red hatched cell in the Main thread lane is a frozen screen; one in the IO or Disk lane is a failure.",
  "track.storage.vz.pf.legend": "Consecutive red hatched cells in the Main thread lane form one blocked stretch: the longer it is, the longer the screen freezes.",
